{"seq":3,"slug":"ideas-and-methods","title":"香农·ideas-and-methods","stage":"DONE","category":"claude-shannon","categoryLabel":"香农","chapterCount":3,"docCount":6,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/claude-shannon/ideas-and-methods","rating":{"composite":3.72,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.4,"coverage":3.25,"positioning":4,"strategic":4.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"hubDir":"/Users/wangyang.learnwy/learnwy/learnwy/l-doc-hub/hubs/famous-people/19_claude-shannon/3_ideas-and-methods","introHtml":"<h1 id=\"香农的思想方法\">香农的思想方法</h1><p>我们已经习惯了用&quot;比特&quot;来谈论一切：一张照片有多少 MB、一条网络的带宽是多少 Gbps、一段密码有多少位。这些日常说法背后，站着同一个人——香农。这个 facet 不重复他的生平，也不罗列他的荣誉，而是专门拆解一件事：他到底是&quot;怎么想&quot;的，才把&quot;信息&quot;这个看似虚无缥缈的东西，变成了可以测量、可以压缩、可以纠错、可以加密的工程对象。</p>\n<p>香农的方法有一条贯穿始终的主线：先剥离，再建模，最后求极限。面对一个混乱的工程问题，他总是先问&quot;哪些东西其实无关&quot;，把意义、内容、语义统统扔掉，只留下&quot;消息从一组可能性中被选出来&quot;这个骨架；然后用概率和对数给这个骨架配一把尺子，也就是熵；最后他不满足于&quot;能做到什么&quot;，而是追问&quot;理论上最多能做到什么&quot;，于是有了信道容量、香农极限这些不可逾越的边界。</p>\n<p>这种做法在他手里反复出现。1937 年的硕士论文里，他把继电器电路的开与关，剥离成布尔代数的真与假，于是电路设计第一次有了可以演算的数学。1948 年的《通信的数学理论》里，他把通信剥离成信源、信道、噪声三块，于是有了信息论。1949 年讨论保密系统时，他又用同一把刀，证明了&quot;绝对安全&quot;到底需要什么代价。</p>\n<p>这个 facet 面向任何对&quot;清晰思考&quot;感兴趣的读者——你不需要是通信工程师，但读完之后，你会更理解为什么&quot;信息&quot;可以被当成一种物理量来对待。三章按由具体到抽象的顺序展开：先看他如何为信息找到一把尺子（度量信息），再看他如何为这把尺子划出物理边界（信道与编码），最后退一步看他真正的方法论遗产——抽象的力量。</p>\n<p>如果你想先了解这些思想是在怎样的人生与年代里诞生的，可以读<a href=\"../life-and-times/bell-labs-years/the-birth-of-information-theory\">信息论的诞生</a>；如果你更关心它们作为&quot;成果&quot;的清单与定位，可以读<a href=\"../core-contributions/founding-information-theory/the-father-of-information-theory\">核心贡献</a>。本 facet 关心的，是这些成果背后那台思考机器是如何运转的。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"measuring-information","title":"度量信息","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/claude-shannon/ideas-and-methods/measuring-information","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"information-as-uncertainty","title":"信息即不确定性","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/claude-shannon/ideas-and-methods/measuring-information/information-as-uncertainty"},{"seq":2,"slug":"the-bit-as-unit","title":"比特：信息的计量单位","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/claude-shannon/ideas-and-methods/measuring-information/the-bit-as-unit"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"channels-and-coding","title":"信道与编码","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/claude-shannon/ideas-and-methods/channels-and-coding","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"channel-capacity","title":"信道容量：传输的物理极限","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/claude-shannon/ideas-and-methods/channels-and-coding/channel-capacity"},{"seq":2,"slug":"reliable-communication","title":"可靠的通信：把差错率逼到零","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/claude-shannon/ideas-and-methods/channels-and-coding/reliable-communication"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"the-power-of-abstraction","title":"抽象的力量","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/claude-shannon/ideas-and-methods/the-power-of-abstraction","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"separating-information-from-meaning","title":"将信息与意义分离","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/claude-shannon/ideas-and-methods/the-power-of-abstraction/separating-information-from-meaning"},{"seq":2,"slug":"mathematical-elegance","title":"以简驭繁：香农的数学审美与构造性思维","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/claude-shannon/ideas-and-methods/the-power-of-abstraction/mathematical-elegance"}]}]}